                <pb facs="0717" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 417.00/43.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Does the wording “by the present Nicaraguan Government,” in article 6, apply to
                    the Government of President Estrada? The Nicaraguan Government fears this
                    paragraph would require reinstatement of the concession of the Bluefields
                    Steamship Co., with its exclusive right of navigating Escondido River, of the
                    lottery concession, and of other concessions referred to in the ministers
                    dispatch 52, of May 25.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
